   "subject": "fieldMask applied to thermal images",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "Hi Filipe, I hope you are doing well.<div><br></div><div>I&#39;ve been trying use thermal images into a fieldMask function to remove the soil background. However, I&#39;ve faced with the follow error message: &quot;<i>At least 3 bands (RGB) are necessary to calculate indices available in FIELDimageR</i>&quot;. Could you please help me with this? I&#39;m attaching an image as example.</div><div><br></div><div>Thanks,</div><div>Marcelo</div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "TsCIKzT4AQAJ",
   "from": "Noah Fahlgren",
   "author": "11b19b85b737e07f",
   "date": "2023-06-19T22:06:34Z",
   "subject": "Re: fieldMask applied to thermal images",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "Hi Marcelo,<div><br></div><div>fieldMask minimally requires RGB data because the indices used for soil masking contain at least some of those channels. See the list of indices in Indicies.txt (<a href=\"https://github.com/OpenDroneMap/FIELDimageR/blob/master/inst/extdata/Indices.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/OpenDroneMap/FIELDimageR/blob/master/inst/extdata/Indices.txt&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793241828454000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0g3XNCbGSIdO7K9sCBV8vg\">https://github.com/OpenDroneMap/FIELDimageR/blob/master/inst/extdata/Indices.txt</a>)</div><div><br></div><div>Best,</div><div>Noah<br><br></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"auto\" class=\"gmail_attr\">On Saturday, June 17, 2023 at 12:42:03 PM UTC-5 <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">marcel...@gmail.com</a> wrote:<br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\">Hi Filipe, I hope you are doing well.<div><br></div><div>I&#39;ve been trying use thermal images into a fieldMask function to remove the soil background. However, I&#39;ve faced with the follow error message: &quot;<i>At least 3 bands (RGB) are necessary to calculate indices available in FIELDimageR</i>&quot;. Could you please help me with this? I&#39;m attaching an image as example.</div><div><br></div><div>Thanks,</div><div>Marcelo</div></blockquote></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "4VpBKeJUAAAJ",
   "from": "fmatias",
   "author": "c59b667c61f258ae",
   "date": "2023-07-08T18:18:55Z",
   "subject": "Re: fieldMask applied to thermal images",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "Hi everyone,<div><br></div><div>You also can trick the function by using the same layer number for all parameters and using only 1 layer on &quot;myIndex&quot;. Please, check the example below:</div><div><br></div><div><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,&quot;SF Mono&quot;,Menlo,Consolas,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,monospace;font-size:13.6px;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px;padding:16px;overflow:auto;line-height:1.45;border-radius:6px;word-break:normal\"><b><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,255);box-sizing:border-box\">EX1.RemSoil</span> <font color=\"#0000ff\"><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box\">&lt;-</span> fieldMask(<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box\">mosaic</span> <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box\">=</span> <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box\">EX1.Rotated</span>, <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box\">Red</span> <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box\">=</span> <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box\">1</span>, <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box\">Green</span> <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box\">=</span> 1, <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box\">Blue</span> <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box\">=</span> 1, myI<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box\">ndex</span> <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box\">=</span> <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box\"><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box\">&quot;Red</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box\">&quot;,</span></span></font></b></span><b><font color=\"#0000ff\"><span style=\"font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,&quot;SF Mono&quot;,Menlo,Consolas,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,monospace;font-size:13.6px;box-sizing:border-box\">cropValue</span><span style=\"font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,&quot;SF Mono&quot;,Menlo,Consolas,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,monospace;font-size:13.6px\"> </span><span style=\"font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,&quot;SF Mono&quot;,Menlo,Consolas,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,monospace;font-size:13.6px;box-sizing:border-box\">=</span><span style=\"font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,&quot;SF Mono&quot;,Menlo,Consolas,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,monospace;font-size:13.6px\"> </span><span style=\"font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,&quot;SF Mono&quot;,Menlo,Consolas,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,monospace;font-size:13.6px;box-sizing:border-box\">0.7</span><span style=\"font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,&quot;SF Mono&quot;,Menlo,Consolas,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,monospace;font-size:13.6px\">, </span><span style=\"font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,&quot;SF Mono&quot;,Menlo,Consolas,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,monospace;font-size:13.6px;box-sizing:border-box\">cropAbove</span><span style=\"font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,&quot;SF Mono&quot;,Menlo,Consolas,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,monospace;font-size:13.6px\"> </span><span style=\"font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,&quot;SF Mono&quot;,Menlo,Consolas,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,monospace;font-size:13.6px;box-sizing:border-box\">=</span><span style=\"font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,&quot;SF Mono&quot;,Menlo,Consolas,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,monospace;font-size:13.6px\"> </span><span style=\"font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,&quot;SF Mono&quot;,Menlo,Consolas,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,monospace;font-size:13.6px;box-sizing:border-box\">T)</span></font></b></div><div><br></div><div>Attention: You need to change the &quot;cropValue&quot; according to your thermal image pixel values.</div><div><br></div><div>Hope it helps...!</div><div><br></div><div>Best,</div><div>Filipe</div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div><br><br></div><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"auto\" class=\"gmail_attr\">Em segunda-feira, 19 de junho de 2023 às 19:06:34 UTC-3, <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">nfah...@danforthcenter.org</a> escreveu:<br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\">Hi Marcelo,<div><br></div><div>fieldMask minimally requires RGB data because the indices used for soil masking contain at least some of those channels. See the list of indices in Indicies.txt (<a href=\"https://github.com/OpenDroneMap/FIELDimageR/blob/master/inst/extdata/Indices.txt\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/OpenDroneMap/FIELDimageR/blob/master/inst/extdata/Indices.txt&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793241828457000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0AfYjybu7pn0G2NjPducp4\">https://github.com/OpenDroneMap/FIELDimageR/blob/master/inst/extdata/Indices.txt</a>)</div><div><br></div><div>Best,</div><div>Noah<br><br></div><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"auto\" class=\"gmail_attr\">On Saturday, June 17, 2023 at 12:42:03 PM UTC-5 <a rel=\"nofollow\">marcel...@gmail.com</a> wrote:<br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\">Hi Filipe, I hope you are doing well.<div><br></div><div>I&#39;ve been trying use thermal images into a fieldMask function to remove the soil background. However, I&#39;ve faced with the follow error message: &quot;<i>At least 3 bands (RGB) are necessary to calculate indices available in FIELDimageR</i>&quot;. Could you please help me with this? I&#39;m attaching an image as example.</div><div><br></div><div>Thanks,</div><div>Marcelo</div></blockquote></div></blockquote></div>"
